{
  "summary": "The app’s UI follows the DESIGN.md specifications in the primary flow and meets accessibility standards (axe score 0, Lighthouse accessibility 98). All major screens (PolicyGate, Dashboard, ReceiptEntry, MileageEntry, Settings, Categories) load, render their default states and support navigation via the always‑visible BottomTabBar and the FAB. Design tokens from src/theme.ts are used throughout the component wrappers, and the mobile‑first layout (SafeAreaView + ScrollView with 16 dp horizontal padding, 420 dp max width) is respected. Interaction states for Buttons, FABs and Switches are defined, and visible focus outlines are applied on web. However, several secondary states required by the spec are not implemented or are incomplete, which warrants medium‑severity findings. No high‑severity blocker (e.g., missing loading/empty state or accessibility‑breaking issue) was found.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The spec defines an \"Error\" state for PolicyGate (full‑screen error view with a Retry button) when storing the acceptance fails, but the current implementation only shows the default and loading states.",
      "fix": "Add an error UI branch that displays a full‑screen view with the message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a retry button that re‑attempts the acceptance storage. Ensure the retry button is focusable and announces the retry action for screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Save error\" state (Snackbar with the message \"Unable to save receipt. Please try again.\") is referenced in the design spec but not present in the component – failures from the receipt store are currently swallowed silently.",
      "fix": "Wrap the save operation in a try/catch, and on catch display a <Snackbar> with the prescribed error message, proper `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"`, and a dismiss action. Reset the loading state of the Save button after the Snackbar is shown."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"OCR no data\" alert dialog (message \"No details could be extracted – please enter manually.\") is missing; when the OCR service returns no fields the UI proceeds as if data were present.",
      "fix": "Detect an empty OCR result and render an <AlertDialog> (or <Dialog>) with the required message and an \"OK\" button. The dialog should trap focus and be announced via `announceForAccessibility`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/OfflineBanner.tsx",
      "issue": "The design calls for a full‑screen offline indicator banner on any screen where a network connection is required, but no such component exists in the repository.",
      "fix": "Create an `OfflineBanner` component that subscribes to NetInfo, renders a full‑width banner with the copy \"You are offline. Some actions require an internet connection.\" and uses `role=\"alert\"`. Include it at the top of screens that perform network‑dependent actions (e.g., Export, Backup)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FABs lack a visible focus outline for keyboard navigation on web, which violates the spec’s focus‑visible requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` rule that applies a 2 dp outline (`borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.outline`) when `focused` or `focusVisible` is true. Ensure the component forwards the `onFocus`/`onBlur` events to manage this state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Delete all data\" row is not styled with the error colour defined in the design tokens (`theme.colors.error`) and may not have the required preceding Divider.",
      "fix": "Wrap the row in a `<List.Item>` with `titleStyle={{ color: theme.colors.error }}` and add a `<Divider />` immediately before it. Verify the row’s text matches the spec exactly (\"Delete all data\")."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom padding for the recent‑activity list is set to 80 dp, which does not provide the required 96 dp (FAB height 56 dp + margin 40 dp). This can cause the list content to be partially obscured by the mini‑FABs.",
      "fix": "Adjust the `contentContainerStyle` of the `<ScrollView>` to `paddingBottom: 96` (using `theme.spacing * 12`). Test on both phone and tablet viewports to confirm the FABs never overlap content."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The DatePicker for receipts does not enforce the \"disable future dates\" rule; users can select dates beyond today.",
      "fix": "Pass `maximumDate={new Date()}` (or a custom prop `disabledFuture={true}`) to the `DatePickerModal` and ensure the UI displays the appropriate helper text. Add a unit test to verify future dates are disabled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button’s loading state does not hide the label text – the spec expects the label to be hidden while the spinner shows.",
      "fix": "When `loading` is true, render only the `<ActivityIndicator />` inside the button and conditionally omit the children text. Ensure the button’s height remains constant to avoid layout shift."
    }
  ]
}

